Stockfish (https://github.com/official-stockfish/Stockfish, GPL-3.0) is installed into the builder and api container images as the
  official release binary, unmodified, and run as a separate process. Its source for the release used (sf_19) is at
  https://github.com/official-stockfish/Stockfish/releases/tag/sf_19 ; its licence text is in that release's Copying.txt.

Maia-3 (https://github.com/CSSLab/maia3, GNU AGPL v3): the `maia3` package and the Maia-3 weights are downloaded at install and run
  time, not stored in this repository. Using them in the api service is why this project is under the AGPL (see below).
  What was checked (2026-11): the repository's LICENSE is the AGPL v3 text, and the 79M model card says "AGPLv3". The 5M and 23M
  cards (the 23M model made the shipped dataset) say "CC BY 4.0 (paper); see repo for code/weights license" and name no weights
  licence of their own, so this project treats all Maia-3 weights as AGPL-3.0. That is a reading, not a statement by the authors.
  The dataset stores only move probabilities computed with the model, not the weights.

Not bundled, used when you run the pipeline or the api yourself (each keeps its own licence): python-chess (GPL-3.0-or-later),
  PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause), Starlette (BSD-3-Clause), uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause), and for the browser tests Playwright (Apache-2.0).

Maia-2 (https://github.com/CSSLab/maia2, MIT): optional alternative backend; its weights have no stated licence and are downloaded, not bundled.

Lichess open database (https://database.lichess.org, CC0 1.0): the games the dataset positions come from.

